AB  - Multimodal Large Language Models (MLLMs) are adept at handling complex tasks involving visual and textual data. However, existing Mamba-based MLLMs face significant challenges in visual feature extraction, leading to suboptimal cross-modal alignment and compromised performance. This paper introduces EM-Mamba, a structured state-space model framework integrating three innovations: dynamic cluster scanning for effectively capturing local and global features, Mamba-Transformer block for efficient cross-modal interaction, and shared-specialized feed-forward mechanisms for modality-specific feature extraction. Experiments on benchmarks such as VQAv2 and GQA demonstrate that EM-Mamba’s accuracy is 3.12 % to 4.0 % higher than the Mamba-based baseline, Cobra, and improves inference speed by 20.1 %. This work advances multimodal efficiency by synergizing state-space models with clustering and hybrid attention.
