AB  - Point clouds are a core Construction 4.0 data modality, enabling dense 3D capture across the project life cycle. However, real-world construction scans are often noisy, incomplete, and semantically limited, making manual interpretation time-consuming and costly. Following PRISMA 2020, this paper reviews 94 journal articles published between 2016 and 2025 and indexed in Scopus and Web of Science on deep learning for construction point-cloud processing. A task-oriented taxonomy is developed to link construction objectives with processing tasks, workflow positions, dataset sources, and deliverable readiness. It further compares major model families according to construction-specific constraints and downstream outputs. Finally, reported barriers are synthesized and research directions are outlined to advance end-to-end, deliverable-oriented automation.
